WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.500
Good morning Hank, it's question Tuesday

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.000
On Wednesday

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.540
The day where I answer real questions from real Nerdfighters

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.760
Hank, yesterday I sent out a tweet asking Nerdfighters

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.700
if they had any questions and they answered on mass.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.780
Right. So most of them were about college.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.140
Having both attended college and watched the movie "Animal House"

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.100
I feel like college is one of my fields of expertise

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.900
and so far as I can tell there are 5 facets of the collegiate experience.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:36.960
Alright so lets take these in order:

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.580
Number 1: Academics. I am going to tell you a secret.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:46.500
Every year many, many, stupid people graduate from college.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:47.920
And if they can do it

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:48.820
so can you.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:54.600
In fact I would argue that it is not that difficult to skate by at most colleges.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.500
That said it turns out to be a huge mistake

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.760
to ignore the academic facets of college;

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.000
partly because the point of life is to engage as deeply as possible

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.260
with the miracle of human consciousness

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.600
and partly because there will come a day where you are 35 years old

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.200
and you are writing a check

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:08.860
every

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.360
single

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:09.860
month

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.140
to pay off your student loans

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.100
and it would be very helpful to you if you  feel like that money bought something.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.000
Because my friends I am here to tell you

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.520
that you do not have to be a college student to play beer pong.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.420
So study. And the only other piece, back into my advice, is to study broadly.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.140
I think its really valuable to take classes in lots of different departments

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.700
because you'll be surprised how the classes you don't think you're interested in

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.300
end up shaping your life.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.420
For example, although I'm not a sci-ency person I took several biology classes in college

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.620
including one called: "AIDS, Ebola, and Emerging Viruses"

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:42.760
and it is of a direct result of that class that today I am a hypochondriac.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.880
Number 2:  Interpersonal relationships

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.000
So most people, when they start college they're pretty worried about making friends.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.240
So here's some advice,

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.200
first be nice to every one. Also, just be calm,

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.940
Like I dont know if this is true for any one else, but when I get into social situations

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.720
where I feel uncomfortable I can be a little bit like:

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.440
[ Insane sounds ] HELLO HELLO I'M JOHN GREEN

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.960
[ More insane sounds ]

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.180
I WANNA BE FRIENDS! I wanna be friends. I wanna be friends.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.700
I cant hide it. I cant hide it. Oh my God I want to be friends with you so bad.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.700
And uh that's scary for people.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.020
Umm a couple other things. Never refer to kissing as scoring

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.700
Never refer to the ladies as "The Ladies"

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.240
And uh, try not to pee or throw up on anyone else or their belongings.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:20.320
I realize that's pretty base level advice for those of us who are potty trained

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.600
but you would be astonished how many people have difficulty following that advice

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.220
during college -- Which brings me to binge drinking.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.320
sometimes there seems to be only 2 types of college students these days.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.720
Those who binge drink with alarming frequency

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:35.680
and those who define themselves primarily in opposition to that binge drinking.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.480
I would submit that neither of these worldviews are particularly attractive.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.160
I mean no one likes a holier-than-thou judgementalist

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.460
but on the other hand no one likes to vomited upon.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.000
That's not true John.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:45.500
Well it should be.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.520
But let me encourage all college students to embrace identities that don't involve alcohol.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.200
Like just join some clubs or something. there are so many clubs in college.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.260
Thats something else I would say; join clubs

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.000
but not just one club. People who belong to just one club

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.260
are super annoying.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.980
Cause they'll never shut up about their one club like it the only one club that matters

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.860
like the only place that needs to be free is Tibet

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:08.720
I love you Tibet, it's nothing personal. I just also love Burma

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.180
4: Road Trips

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:11.740
Take them.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.640
And lastly: Living on your own except not really because you don't have to clean the toilets.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.800
I'm not going to tell you life in college is easy

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.520
or give you any of the lies how its going to be the best years of your life.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.460
Which it wont unless you have a terrible, terrible life.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.680
But the great thing about college is that it creates this weird in-between space

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.360
where you're no longer a child but you also don't have to do all of the annoying things

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.480
about being an adult like cleaning your own toilets.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.100
Well you don't if you don't have a dorm room. Sorry for people who don't have dorm rooms

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.560
because now I'm just taunting you.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:41.740
but this in-between space gives you, for the first time in your life, time to pick what you want to do.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.780
So you can read  Foucault and talk about Foucault with some of the smartest people you'll ever meet

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.080
And you can also skip a biology test to drive to the Grand Canyon with a girl you met the day before.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.120
Don't let the freedom of that moment get by you.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.960
So that's my-- oh and one other thing, don't get too excited about the fountainhead.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.560
Hank I'll see you on Friday

